import{_ as o,o as t,c as r,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CyZTVJbV.js";const v=JSON.parse('{"title":"","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"announcements/v1.22/x-thread-en.md","filePath":"announcements/v1.22/x-thread-en.md"}'),i={name:"announcements/v1.22/x-thread-en.md"};function n(s,e,c,d,l,p){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<p>1/ kiwa v1.22 is out — Auth 深化 II milestone. After v1.21&#39;s Auth 深化 (4 protocol adapters as pure mocks), v1.22 layers <strong>real drivers</strong> on top — Keycloak testcontainers (OIDC + Federation), oauth2-mock-server testcontainers (OAuth 2.1), Chrome caBLE hybrid transport (Passkey). Mocks stay the first-line contract, real drivers become the second-line fidelity check. Zero regression to the &lt; 5 ms per test mock latency budget.</p><p>2/ 3 execution modes SSOT (<code>docs/concepts/real-driver-testing.md</code>) — <code>mock only</code> (default, <code>KIWA_MODE</code> unset) = pure <code>@kiwa/auth</code> mock, 0 network, ~1 ms per test. Every PR runs this. <code>real-optional</code> (<code>KIWA_MODE=real-optional</code>) = try real driver, fall back to mock with a warning. Laptop-friendly. <code>real-required</code> (<code>KIWA_MODE=real</code> + <code>KEYCLOAK_URL</code> / <code>OAUTH21_BOOTSTRAP=1</code> / Chrome caBLE flag) = fail hard if driver missing; nightly CI + pre-release smoke.</p><p>3/ v1.22-1 dogfood-oidc-federation gains a Keycloak testcontainers real driver. Docker Keycloak 26 boot + realm import + client registration + JWKS endpoint + Federation trust anchor. The v1.21-4 fidelity harness 16 axes get real coverage; axes 1 (Discovery metadata) + 3 (JWKS rotation with kid rollover) both record live matches against Keycloak. <code>.well-known/openid-configuration</code> fields match one-to-one between mock and real.</p><p>4/ v1.22-2 dogfood-oauth21-provider gains an oauth2-mock-server testcontainers real driver. 5 endpoint (/authorize + /token + /revoke + /userinfo + /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server) + PKCE S256 + DPoP + refresh rotation + revocation cascade all get live coverage. Bug 1 fix: /authorize post-adapter error redirect (RFC 6749 §4.1.2.1) was returning inconsistent state parameter — v1.22-2 flipped the mock to match the RFC + real oauth2-mock-server behaviour.</p><p>5/ v1.22-3 dogfood-oidc-federation Nuxt 3 RP full flow + a11y axe-core gate. RP journey: login button → OP redirect → callback → userinfo panel → logout. Playwright + <code>@axe-core/playwright</code> for WCAG 2.1 AA + WAI-ARIA authoring practice. Release gate 7-axis a11y branch flips from N/A (v1.21 skeleton) to PASS (v1.22 full interactive surface). Every WCAG blocker gets a per-rule reason for triage.</p><p>6/ v1.22-4 dogfood-webauthn-passkey-app caBLE hybrid transport 5-axis fidelity harness. CTAP2 hybrid transport (Cloud-Assisted BLE) real device flow: QR gen + BLE handshake + WebSocket tunnel + credential migration + signature roundtrip. Playwright + Chrome <code>--enable-features=WebAuthenticationRemoteDesktopSupport</code>. 40 new tests covering the 5 axes against <code>@kiwa/auth</code>&#39;s new caBLE mock — phone → laptop credential migration works whether the mock is driving or a real Chrome + Android phone pair is.</p><p>7/ v1.22-5 Federation JWKS rotation real e2e — real Keycloak OP + Nuxt 3 RP + real JWKS endpoint (public URL + HTTP cache invalidation). kid rotation → RP-side JWKS refresh → id_token verify continue as a single end-to-end chain across a real network. Axes 4a-4d (inside window / past retention / multi-rotation retention / fresh active key after rotation) all get real coverage. Fidelity gate PASS = mock never drifts silently from real Keycloak.</p><p>8/ 1 npm minor bump — <code>@kiwa/auth</code> v0.4.0 → v0.5.0 published to npm. Additive-only: v1.21 setup entry points keep their signatures, v1.22 adds <code>realDriver</code> option + caBLE methods alongside. docs: 2 tutorials (37 real driver testing + 38 Passkey caBLE flow) + additive migration v1.21 → v1.22 + concept doc <code>real-driver-testing.md</code> (3 execution modes SSOT + fidelity axis catalog). VitePress + gh-pages published. Roadmap: <a href="https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://github.com/cardene777/kiwa#roadmap</a> — v1.11 → v1.12 → v1.13 → v1.14 → v1.15 → v1.16 → v1.17 → v1.18 → v1.19 → v1.20 → v1.21 → v1.22: 12 milestones in a row.</p>',8)])])}const u=o(i,[["render",n]]);export{v as __pageData,u as default};
